#13500
An Old and Forgotten Passage~
   Through a narrow opening, you find a small chamber in the brick foundation
beneath the temple. These bricks, smoothed and darkened by the ravages of time,
protect a stone floor and part of an older stone wall, intrictately carved,
though most of the details have worn away. It's cool down here. Sand fills the
corners of the floor, long unswept, with only cobwebs to contain it.
~
d 0 0 -1
E
opening up~
The opening is narrow, but you can squeeze through.
~
E
chamber foundation~
It's a rather small chamber in the foundation of the temple.
~
E
temple~
The temple is above you; what's down here seems older.
~
E
stones blocks walls bricks~
   The walls here are made of old brick except for the far wall, which is made
from large stones that meet perfectly at the edges with no mortar.
~
E
sand corners~
Loose sand is strewn about the area and collects in the corners.
~
E
floor down~
The floor is made from large stones.
~
E
cobwebs webs~
Looks like nobody has swept this place out in quite some time.
~
E
light~
The only light here cascades down through the narrow opening.
~
E
carvings carved details reliefs~
   Once, there were intricate scenes carved in bas-relief along the stones of
the far wall. But time has taken its toll, and now all you can make out are
vague man-like shapes in some sort of grand scene, standing before a bull.
Details are better on the bull, whose head is in high relief with one horn
still intact.
   The end of a frayed rope is still tied to the horn.
~
E
rope frayed~
   All that remains of the frayed old rope is the part that's tied to the
bull's horns. No hint of its original purpose remains.
~
E
horns bull sculpture~
   A bit of old frayed rope is tied around one of the horns of a bull
sculpture, carved in high relief from the stone wall.
~
