#13523
A Rancid Pit of Jagged Spikes~
   There is little space to walk between the long black spikes and the bones
scattered among them. The gut-churning smell of rotting flesh is thick; this
pit has fed all too recently. The only hope of escape is the old ladder against
the wall.
~
bdg 0 0 13505
D8
~
0 13524
E
spikes spines jagged black~
   Each spike is nearly as tall as a man, made from some metal too old and
stained to identify. They're attached securely to the floor at different
angles, making it all but impossible to survive a fall -- as witnessed by the
sheer number of bodies.
~
E
bones bodies body corpses flesh rotting~
   It wouldn't be a simple task to count the number of bodies in this foul pit,
not least because most have decayed away to bones. Some bodies are fresher, but
fresh is certainly not the way you'd describe them due to the sheer number of
maggots.
~
E
pit~
   The pit slopes down at such a steep angle that the walls cannot be climbed.
It's square in shape, but you can't tell quite how tall it is. There's only
darkness above.
~
E
ladder~
The old metal ladder has a pale green color. It seems sturdy enough.
~
E
walls stones~
   The enormous stones of the wall are cut at a slight angle -- enough to
funnel unwary adventurers down to the spikes; too steep to climb again. The
stones are cut to such a precise shape that there is no mortar between them,
and no gap where a finger could find traction.
~
E
down floor~
Bones litter the floor between the spikes.
~
E
up~
A ladder extends up into the darkness.
~
